{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1940,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Watch what happens when I place some small drops of food coloring on to this slide."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8280,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some are attracted to each other and merge,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11140,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while others repel and chase each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15200,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It looks just like the tiny world of micro-organisms, but why?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19680,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well if you want to try this out for yourself"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21640,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You need to get some ordinary food coloring and dilute it with distilled water using a pipette."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26300,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then pass the microscope slide through a flame for about thirty seconds."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30220,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let it cool, and then put some drops of different concentration on to the slide."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35800,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You'll find that drops of similar concentration attract each other and merge"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39640,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while drops of different concentrations chase each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69460,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can draw guides on the slide using permanent marker, which is hydrophobic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73220,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and set up long distance pursuits."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78680,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or you can find that drops of similar concentration attract each other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81880,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "despite the hydrophobic barriers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85440,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how is this possible just using ordinary food coloring and water?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90020,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well the key is evaporation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92080,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Each drop is constantly evaporating, so around it is an envelope of vapour."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96860,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The rate of evaporation depends on the humidity around the drop"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100160,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the drier the air is, the faster the rate of evaporation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103940,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when any two drops are close enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105600,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the humidity between them is greater than than the humidity around them,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109460,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and therefore there's more evaporation around the droplets"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112360,
    "dDurationMs": 980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then in-between them,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113340,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this pushes them together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115540,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So differential evaporation makes the droplets attract,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118520,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but that's not the whole story."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120340,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Food coloring is a mixture of mainly two molecules,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123580,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "water and propylene glycol."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125920,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These two liquids mix well so we say they are miscible,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129000,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but they have different properties."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130880,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, water evaporates more readily because its lighter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134420,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it has a stronger surface tension due to hydrogen bonding."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138100,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is important because interesting things happen when there are gradients in surface tension."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143440,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, if I add some pepper to this bowl of water to allow me to see the motion,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148880,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then I add a little dab of soap, right in the middle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153640,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you see that all of the water rushes outwards,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157100,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this is because soap has a lower surface tension than water."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160980,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can think of it a bit like a tug of war."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163200,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Before I added the soap all of those water molecules were pulling on each other equally,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167720,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but once I add the soap molecules in the middle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170080,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their weaker surface tension means the water molecules around them are pulling"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174180,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "harder on each other than the soap is,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176220,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so they rush outwards away from that spreading soap drop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180040,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this motion is called \"Marangoni flow.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183140,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And a similar thing is actually happening with our food coloring droplets."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187140,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you have drops of similar concentration they attract each other due to the higher humidity in-between them,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191960,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they merge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192960,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And although drops of different concentration also attract each other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196380,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they don't merge when they come into contact."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198600,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is because the water in the lower concentration drop"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200960,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pulls together and away from the drop with the higher concentration of propylene glycol,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205600,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just like with the soap and water."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207520,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And differential evaporation drives the two drops forwards."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210980,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is fascinating to watch these droplets and think about how closely their motion mimics life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216920,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Living organisms seek out molecules like food,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220420,
    "dDurationMs": 2620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this is a process known as \"chemotaxis.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223040,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what these droplets are doing is really not all that dissimilar,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226400,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in fact its been called artificial chemotaxis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229880,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as amazingly life like as their motion appears,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 233700,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a way, I think it shouldn't be all that surprising."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237080,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After all, evolution began with the natural tendencies of molecules:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241980,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to form and break apart, to attract and repel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245580,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then over billions of years of refinement through natural selection,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 249420,
    "dDurationMs": 3020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "evolution has produced bodies whose utilisation of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252440,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these natural tendencies of molecules appears miraculous."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257280,
    "dDurationMs": 2380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And its that,  that we call life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261940,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I tried using slides that hadn't been passed through a flame"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 265980,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then I couldn't get the drops to move."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268960,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So on researching this further I found out that passing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272040,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the microscope slide through the flame creates a high energy sufrace"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275960,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and what that means is, the flame is essentially breaking open some of the bonds -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281220,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the glass bonds in the surface of this slide -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284020,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and when you put the droplet on top,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287780,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Its those open bonds, its that high energy surface that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290520,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "draws some of the water molecules away from the droplet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293400,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that actually makes the water molecule more likely to evaporate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296940,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But as just happened right there, some of the microscopes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299980,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some of the microscope slides have shattered."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302340,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so you should be particularly careful when doing this procedure,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 305620,
    "dDurationMs": 4900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "obviously heating them up to a very high temperature causes them to expand a lot"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310520,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and when they contract again as they're cooling, well then,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314420,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they sometimes break apart because of those stresses."
    } ]
  } ]
}
